  "model_id": "ecmwf-ifs-ens",
  "model_name": "ECMWF IFS ENS",
  "description_summary": "This dataset is an archive of past and present ECMWF IFS ENS forecasts at 0.1 degree resolution, optimized for spatial (map) access patterns. Forecasts are identified by an initialization time (`init_time`) denoting the start time of the model run as well as by the `ensemble_member`, and step forward along the `lead_time` dimension out to 15 days. This dataset contains the 00 and 12 UTC initialization times, which produce the full length 15 day forecast.\n\nVariables on pressure levels live in the `pressure_level` group.\n\nNote: `dynamical-catalog>=1.0.0` (or `zarr>=3.2 icechunk>=2.0 gribberish>=1.7`) is required.",
  "description_details": "### Source\n\nThe source grib files this archive references are provided by [ECMWF Open Data](https://www.ecmwf.int/en/forecasts/datasets/open-data). Data is read directly from ECMWF's copy on Google Cloud (`gs://ecmwf-open-data`) and AWS Open Data (`s3://ecmwf-forecasts`).\n\nECMWF does not provide user support for the free & open datasets. Users should refer to the public [User Forum](https://forum.ecmwf.int/) for any questions related to the source material.\n\n### Model updates\n\nIFS is updated regularly. Find details of recent and upcoming\n[changes to the forecasting system](https://confluence.ecmwf.int/display/FCST/Changes+to+the+forecasting+system)\non the ECMWF website.\n\n### Storage\n\nStorage for this dataset is generously provided by [AWS Open Data](https://aws.amazon.com/opendata/).\n\n### Chunks\n\nThis dataset is stored in [Zarr](https://zarr.dev/) format, which splits each variable into a grid of **chunks** \u2014 the smallest unit read from storage. When possible, aligning your reads with this dataset's chunk grid can significantly improve data access speed.\n\nThe element count and coordinate span of this dataset:\n\n| dimension | chunk |\n|---|---|\n| init_time | 1 (12 hours) |\n| lead_time | 1 (~3 hours) |\n| ensemble_member | 1 |\n| latitude | 1801 (180.1\u00b0) |\n| longitude | 3600 (360\u00b0) |\n| **uncompressed** | 49.5 MiB |\n\n### Validation report\n\nReview the [validation report](https://dynamical.org/catalog/ecmwf-ifs-ens-forecast-15-day-0-1-degree-virtual/validation/) for variable availability, missing data, known quirks, fill values, value distributions, and sample plots.",
  "description_model": "The Integrated Forecasting System (IFS) is a global forecast model developed by ECMWF. ENS is an ensemble configuration of IFS: 51 ensemble members in the medium range and 101 in the sub-seasonal (extended) range. IFS consists of a numerical model of the Earth system, which includes an atmospheric model at its heart, coupled with models of other Earth system components such as the ocean. The data assimilation system combines the latest weather observations with a recent forecast to obtain the best possible estimate of the current state of the Earth system.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Global average temperature, control member",
      "variants": [
        {
          "label": "dynamical-catalog",
          "code": "import dynamical_catalog  # dynamical-catalog>=1.0.0\n\nds = dynamical_catalog.open(\"ecmwf-ifs-ens-forecast-15-day-0-1-degree-virtual\", chunks=None)\nds[\"temperature_2m\"].sel(init_time=\"2026-11-01T00\", lead_time=\"24h\", ensemble_member=0).mean()\n\n# Variables with a vertical dimension live in the pressure_level group\nds_pressure = dynamical_catalog.open(\"ecmwf-ifs-ens-forecast-15-day-0-1-degree-virtual\", group=\"pressure_level\", chunks=None)\nds_pressure[\"geopotential_height\"].sel(init_time=\"2026-11-01T00\", lead_time=\"120h\", pressure_level=500, ensemble_member=0).mean()",
          "language": "python"
        },
        {
          "label": "pystac",
          "code": "import icechunk\nimport pystac\nimport xarray as xr\n\ncatalog = pystac.Catalog.from_file(\"https://stac.dynamical.org/catalog.json\")\ncollection = catalog.get_child(\"ecmwf-ifs-ens-forecast-15-day-0-1-degree-virtual\")\nasset = collection.assets[\"icechunk-https\"]\n\nauthorize = icechunk.containers_credentials({\"gs://ecmwf-open-data/\": icechunk.gcs_credentials(anonymous=True), \"s3://ecmwf-forecasts/\": icechunk.s3_anonymous_credentials()})\nrepo = icechunk.Repository.open(\n    icechunk.http_storage(asset.href),\n    authorize_virtual_chunk_access=authorize,\n)\nsession = repo.readonly_session(\"main\")\n\nds = xr.open_zarr(session.store, chunks=None)\nds[\"temperature_2m\"].sel(init_time=\"2026-11-01T00\", lead_time=\"24h\", ensemble_member=0).mean()\n\n# Variables with a vertical dimension live in the pressure_level group\nds_pressure = xr.open_zarr(session.store, group=\"pressure_level\", chunks=None)\nds_pressure[\"geopotential_height\"].sel(init_time=\"2026-11-01T00\", lead_time=\"120h\", pressure_level=500, ensemble_member=0).mean()",
          "language": "python"
        },
        {
          "label": "prompt",
